Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: a picked folder is a folder.

Arctic: the Common Item Dialog made the ID list of what was typed or
selected from its name alone (SHSimpleIDListFromPath), which carries no
attributes. ReactOS' shell32 answers SFGAO_FOLDER from the ID list itself,
so FOS_PICKFOLDERS refused every folder: "The selection contains a
non-folder object" in any program that chooses a folder. The ID list now
comes from SHParseDisplayName where the path exists.
---
--- a/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
@@ -702,7 +702,13 @@
             filter = fn_iter;
         }
 
-        pidla[i] = SHSimpleIDListFromPath(canon_filename);
+        /* Arctic: the ID list of what is there, read from the disk. One made
+         * from the name alone says nothing of a folder, and ReactOS' shell32
+         * took it for a file: "The selection contains a non-folder object"
+         * on every folder picked. The name alone stays for what is not there
+         * yet, the file a Save dialog makes. */
+        if (FAILED(SHParseDisplayName(canon_filename, NULL, &pidla[i], 0, NULL)))
+            pidla[i] = SHSimpleIDListFromPath(canon_filename);
 
         if(psf_parent && !(open_action == ONOPEN_BROWSE))
             IShellFolder_Release(psf_parent);
